CLASS AppState
    DESCRIPTION: Stores and manages application state loaded from the server
    NAMESPACE: NewgroundsIO
    
    PURPOSE: This class acts as a cache and store for all data loaded from the server.
    Instead of contacting the server every time you need medal info or scoreboard data,
    AppState keeps a local copy that stays synchronized with the server.
    
    WHY NEEDED: Making network requests is SLOW. By caching data locally, we can access it
    instantly. When the server responds with updates, we update the cache in place (using
    observer patterns) so object references stay valid.
    
    ====================
    STATIC READONLY PROPERTIES
    ====================
    
    dataProperties: array = [
        'gatewayVersion',
        'currentVersion',
        'hostApproved',
        'saveSlots',
        'scoreBoards',
        'medals',
        'medalScore'
    ]
        PURPOSE: List of all app state properties that can be loaded from the server
        WHY: Used to validate property names - prevents typos like loadData(['meddles'])
    
    ====================
    PRIVATE PROPERTIES
    ====================
    
    dataLoaded: array = []
        PURPOSE: Tracks which properties have been loaded from the server
        WHY: hasLoaded('medals') checks if this array contains 'medals'
        This lets developers know which data is available to use
    
    core: NewgroundsIO.Core
        PURPOSE: Reference to the Core instance
        WHY: Need Core to queue components and execute requests

    slotListsMerged: Integer = 0
        PURPOSE: How many CloudSave.loadSlots results setValueFromResult() has merged
        WHY: loadData() compares it before and after its request, to tell whether a slot list
        came back at all. See loadData() and mergeWithoutCloudList().

    localSaveSlots: LocalSaveSlotStore
        PURPOSE: The local mirror of this app's save slots
        WHY: A save slot is intended to be stored on the cloud, with a local fallback protecting
        it from network loss and server outages. See SAVE SLOT LOCAL FALLBACK at the end of this
        file. Keep this PRIVATE: the SaveSlot model goes through readLocalSlotData(),
        writeLocalSlotData() and clearLocalSlotData() instead, which keeps the merge in one place.
    
    ====================
    PUBLIC PROPERTIES
    ====================
    
    passportIsOpen: boolean = false
        PURPOSE: Flag indicating whether Passport login window is currently open
        WHY: NGIO.checkSession() uses this flag to decide if it should wait
        before checking the server (user is probably still logging in)

    offerGuestSaves: boolean = true
        PURPOSE: Whether a save made while nobody was signed in (a guest save) becomes the local
        copy of whoever signs in next
        WHY: Some games want a player to keep progress they made before signing in. Others, on
        shared machines, want guest saves kept away from players entirely. When false, guest
        saves stay guest-only and are still there the next time nobody is signed in. Set through
        NGIO.offerGuestSaves. See SAVE SLOT LOCAL FALLBACK.

    ====================
    READONLY PROPERTIES
    ====================
    
    host: string = "N/A"
        PURPOSE: The domain hosting this app (e.g., "uploads.ungrounded.net")
        WHY: Some Newgrounds features are domain-aware. We extract the domain
        from the URL so the server knows where the app is running
    
    sessionStorageKey: string | null = null
        PURPOSE: Unique key for storing the session ID in persistent storage
        WHY: When user closes and reopens the app, we can restore their session
        from persistent storage using this key. Key includes App ID to avoid collisions
        between multiple apps sharing the same domain.
    
    session: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Session
        PURPOSE: The current user session object
        WHY: Contains session ID, user info, expiration time, etc.
        Stores all session-related state
    
    gatewayVersion: string | null = null
        PURPOSE: Version number of the Newgrounds gateway (e.g., "3.2.0")
        WHY: Used to notify developers if the gateway has been updated
    
    currentVersion: string | null = null
        PURPOSE: Latest version of this app as set in Newgrounds project settings
        WHY: Used to check if the user is running an outdated version
        If currentVersion > NGIO.buildVersion, app should notify user to update
    
    clientDeprecated: boolean = false
        PURPOSE: Flag set to true if app version is outdated
        WHY: Developers can check this flag to prompt users to update
        NOTE: Only meaningful once the Newgrounds project has a version set in
        its "Version Control" settings AND core.buildVersion is set. With no
        project version configured, leave core.buildVersion null - the server
        compares the two, and sending a build version with nothing to compare
        against can set this true for a deprecation that isn't real.
    
    hostApproved: boolean = true
        PURPOSE: Whether the domain hosting this app is approved in settings
        WHY: Developers can restrict which domains are allowed to run their app
        If hostApproved=false, app is running on unauthorized domain (possibly hacked copy)
    
    saveSlots: array | null = null
        PURPOSE: Array of SaveSlot objects for cloud saves
        WHY: Stores metadata about cloud save slots (timestamps, filesizes, url of actual data, etc.).
    
    scoreBoards: array | null = null
        PURPOSE: Array of ScoreBoard objects for leaderboards
        WHY: Stores leaderboard data loaded from server
    
    medals: array | null = null
        PURPOSE: Array of Medal objects for achievements
        WHY: Stores medal data loaded from server
    
    medalScore: integer = 0
        PURPOSE: Total points earned from all unlocked medals, across all games
        WHY: Displays user's achievement score
    
    ====================
    CONSTRUCTOR
    ====================
    
    CONSTRUCTOR(core: NewgroundsIO.Core)
        
        PURPOSE: Initialize AppState and attempt to restore previous session if available
        
        PARAMETERS:
            core: The Core instance this AppState is tied to
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Store reference to Core
            SET this.core TO core
            
            COMMENT: Create a new empty Session object
            SET this.session TO new NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Session()
            SET this.session.id TO null
            
            COMMENT: Create unique storage key including app ID
            COMMENT: This prevents different apps from overwriting each other's session data
            SET this.sessionStorageKey TO "ngio-saved-session-id-for-" + core.appId
            
            COMMENT: Try to restore session from persistent storage
            COMMENT: If user has been here before, their session might still be valid
            CREATE savedSessionId AS GET_FROM_PERSISTENT_STORAGE(this.sessionStorageKey)
            IF savedSessionId exists AND savedSessionId is not empty THEN
                COMMENT: Restore the saved session ID
                SET this.session.id TO savedSessionId
            ELSE
                COMMENT: No saved session - try URL query string
                COMMENT: Newgrounds includes session ID in URLs for hosted games
                COMMENT: Example URL: ?ngio_session_id=123456789.aBcdEfG
                CREATE sessionIdFromURL AS EXTRACT_QUERY_PARAMETER("ngio_session_id")
                IF sessionIdFromURL exists AND sessionIdFromURL is not empty THEN
                    SET this.session.preauthenticatedId TO sessionIdFromURL
                    SET this.session.id TO sessionIdFromURL
                END IF
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Determine the domain hosting this app
            IF PLATFORM_SUPPORTS_DOMAIN_DETECTION THEN
                COMMENT: Extract domain from environment (implementation varies by platform)
                COMMENT: See IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE.txt for platform-specific domain detection patterns
                SET this.host TO GET_CURRENT_DOMAIN()
            END IF
    END CONSTRUCTOR
    
    ====================
    PUBLIC METHODS
    ====================
    
    FUNCTION loadData(propertyNames: array, callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)
        
        PURPOSE: Bulk-load app data from the server (medals, scoreboards, versions, etc.)
        WHY: Instead of loading each piece separately, batch them in one request for efficiency
        
        PARAMETERS:
            propertyNames: (required) Array of property names to load (must exist in dataProperties)
            callback: (optional, default: null) Function called when done - receives (appState, error)
            thisArg: (optional, default: null) Context to use when calling the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            appState: (required) AppState - The updated AppState instance
            error: (optional, default: null) Error - Error object if something went wrong
        
        EXPLANATION:
            This method coordinates with Core to:
            1. Validate that requested properties exist
            2. Create appropriate component for each property
            3. Queue all components
            4. Execute them in a single request
            5. Update appState properties with results
            6. Mark properties as loaded
            7. Call the callback
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Validate input
            IF propertyNames is empty THEN
                THROW error "propertyNames array is empty"
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Check that all requested properties are valid
            FOR EACH propertyName IN propertyNames
                IF propertyName NOT in dataProperties THEN
                    THROW error "Unknown property name: " + propertyName
                END IF
            END FOR
            
            COMMENT: Create a component for each property and queue it
            FOR EACH propertyName IN propertyNames
                CREATE component AS null
                
                COMMENT: Determine which component to create based on property name
                SWITCH propertyName
                    CASE 'gatewayVersion':
                        COMMENT: Component to get gateway version info
                        CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("Gateway", "getVersion", null, this.core)
                    
                    CASE 'currentVersion':
                        COMMENT: Component to check for app updates
                        CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("App", "getCurrentVersion", null, this.core)
                        IF component is not null THEN
                            SET component.version TO core.buildVersion
                        END IF
                    
                    CASE 'hostApproved':
                        COMMENT: Component to check if current domain is approved
                        CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("App", "getHostLicense", null, this.core)
                        IF component is not null THEN
                            SET component.host TO this.host
                        END IF
                    
                    CASE 'saveSlots':
                        COMMENT: Component to load cloud save slots
                        CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("CloudSave", "loadSlots", null, this.core)
                    
                    CASE 'medals':
                        COMMENT: Component to load medal list
                        CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("Medal", "getList", null, this.core)
                    
                    CASE 'medalScore':
                        COMMENT: Component to get user's total medal score
                        CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("Medal", "getMedalScore", null, this.core)
                    
                    CASE 'scoreBoards':
                        COMMENT: Component to load scoreboard data
                        CREATE component AS CALL ObjectFactory.CreateComponent("ScoreBoard", "getBoards", null, this.core)
                END SWITCH
                
                COMMENT: Queue the component for execution
                IF component is not null THEN
                    CALL core.queueComponent(component)
                END IF
            END FOR
            
            COMMENT: How many slot lists setValueFromResult() has merged so far, so the
            COMMENT: callback below can tell whether one came back at all.
            CREATE slotListsBefore AS this.slotListsMerged

            COMMENT: Execute all queued components in one request
            CALL core.executeQueue(
                FUNCTION onComplete(response)
                    COMMENT: No slot list came back from the gateway: refused without being
                    COMMENT: sent (nobody signed in), or the request never got there. Neither
                    COMMENT: passes through setValueFromResult(), so the local copies have to
                    COMMENT: be merged here, or a player who starts offline, or a guest, gets
                    COMMENT: no slots at all. That's the case the local copies exist for.
                    IF propertyNames contains 'saveSlots' AND this.slotListsMerged equals slotListsBefore THEN
                        CALL this.mergeWithoutCloudList()
                    END IF

                    COMMENT: A request can fail at THREE independent levels, and all
                    COMMENT: three have to be checked. Checking only the envelope
                    COMMENT: reports a failed load as a successful empty one.
                    COMMENT:
                    COMMENT:   TRANSPORT   no response at all
                    COMMENT:   ENVELOPE    response.success is not true
                    COMMENT:   COMPONENT   an individual result inside a successful
                    COMMENT:               response reports success:false
                    COMMENT:
                    COMMENT: The component level is the one that gets missed, and it is
                    COMMENT: the ORDINARY shape of "you are not logged in". Asking for
                    COMMENT: saveSlots or medalScore without a session returns:
                    COMMENT:
                    COMMENT:   {"success":true,"result":[{"component":"CloudSave.loadSlots",
                    COMMENT:     "data":{"success":false,
                    COMMENT:             "error":{"code":110,"message":"User is not logged in."}}}]}
                    COMMENT:
                    COMMENT: Envelope success, component refusal. Report only the envelope
                    COMMENT: and the game reads the silence as "this user has no saves"
                    COMMENT: rather than "this user is not signed in".
                    COMMENT: Every error set here is a NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Error
                    COMMENT: model - the same type the gateway sends, and the same type
                    COMMENT: NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError() returns. Never a bare string or
                    COMMENT: an ad-hoc object. Its fields that matter: code (an integer,
                    COMMENT: one of the NewgroundsIO.Errors constants) and message (a
                    COMMENT: string). getError(code) fills both in from the code table.
                    CREATE localError AS null

                    IF response is null THEN
                        SET localError TO CALL NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(NewgroundsIO.Errors.INVALID_RESPONSE)
                    ELSE IF response.success is not true THEN
                        IF response.error is not null THEN
                            COMMENT: Already a typed Error model - pass it straight
                            COMMENT: through, do not copy its code/message into a new one.
                            SET localError TO response.error
                        ELSE
                            SET localError TO CALL NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(NewgroundsIO.Errors.INVALID_RESPONSE)
                        END IF
                    ELSE
                        SET localError TO CALL firstResultError(response)
                    END IF

                    COMMENT: Call the developer's callback with results
                    IF callback is not null THEN
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING this, localError
                    END IF
                END FUNCTION
            )

        COMMENT: NOTE: components that DID succeed are still cached, so a partial failure
        COMMENT: is not a total one. hasLoaded() reports which properties actually
        COMMENT: arrived, and it is worth exposing resultErrors() below so a caller can
        COMMENT: see every component that failed rather than only the first.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION resultErrors(response): array

        PURPOSE: List every component inside a successful response that reported failure.
        WHY: One request can carry several components, so "did it work?" is a question
        PER COMPONENT and the answer has to say WHICH one failed. A caller told only
        "something failed" cannot decide whether to retry, prompt for a login, or carry
        on with the parts that loaded.

        RETURNS: An array of {component, error} pairs. Empty when every component
        succeeded, or when the response never got far enough to have components.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE errors AS empty array

            IF response is null OR response.success is not true THEN
                COMMENT: Envelope or transport failure - no component ran, so there is
                COMMENT: nothing at this level to report. The caller handles those.
                RETURN errors
            END IF

            COMMENT: Handle BOTH result shapes. executeQueue always sends the queue as an
            COMMENT: execute LIST, so a response produced by loadData always carries
            COMMENT: `resultList` - even for a single property. But this function is
            COMMENT: public: a caller can hand it a single-component response from
            COMMENT: executeComponent(), which carries the scalar `result` instead.
            COMMENT: Read whichever is populated; reading only `resultList` skips that
            COMMENT: caller silently.
            CREATE results AS the response's result list, or a one-item list holding its
                single result, or an empty list if it has neither

            FOR EACH result IN results
                IF result is null THEN
                    CONTINUE
                END IF

                IF result.success is not true THEN
                    COMMENT: Test success, NOT error. A refused component is not obliged
                    COMMENT: to carry an error object, and testing only `error` lets that
                    COMMENT: case through as a success - the silent failure returning by
                    COMMENT: another route.
                    IF result.error is not null THEN
                        APPEND {component: result's component name, error: result.error} TO errors
                    ELSE
                        APPEND {component: result's component name,
                                error: CALL NewgroundsIO.Errors.getError(NewgroundsIO.Errors.INVALID_RESPONSE)} TO errors
                    END IF
                END IF
            END FOR

            RETURN errors
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION firstResultError(response): NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Error | null

        PURPOSE: The first component-level error in a response, or null if there is none.
        WHY: Thin wrapper over resultErrors(), so callbacks with a single (value, error)
        signature - loadData and everything built on it - keep that signature.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE errors AS CALL resultErrors(response)

            IF errors is empty THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF

            RETURN the `error` of the first entry in errors
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION hasLoaded(propertyName: string): boolean
        
        PURPOSE: Check whether a specific property has been loaded from the server
        WHY: Developers need to know if data is available before trying to use it
        
        PARAMETERS:
            propertyName: Property to check (must be in dataProperties)
        
        RETURNS: true if property has been loaded, false otherwise
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Validate the property name
            IF propertyName NOT in dataProperties THEN
                THROW error "Unknown property name: " + propertyName
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Check if this property is in the loaded list
            IF propertyName in dataLoaded THEN
                RETURN true
            ELSE
                RETURN false
            END IF
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION getSessionStatus(): NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus
        
        PURPOSE: Analyze the current session state and return a SessionStatus object
        WHY: Provides a simple way for developers to understand the session state
        at a glance without digging through properties
        
        RETURNS: SessionStatus object with status code, user (if logged in), and error (if any)
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Create a new SessionStatus to report
            CREATE sessionStatus AS new NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus()
            
            COMMENT: === Check basic session existence ===
            IF session is null OR session.id is empty THEN
                COMMENT: No session yet - return uninitialized status
                RETURN sessionStatus
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: === Check if session is expired ===
            IF session.expired is true THEN
                COMMENT: Session was valid but has now expired
                CALL onSessionCleared()
                SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.EXPIRED
                RETURN sessionStatus
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: === Check for session errors ===
            COMMENT: The server signals a dead session TWO ways: the `expired` flag above,
            COMMENT: and a component failing with EXPIRED_SESSION here. Handling only the
            COMMENT: first leaves EXPIRED nearly unreachable in practice, because a
            COMMENT: rejected id never sets the flag - it returns this error instead.
            IF session.error is not null THEN
                COMMENT: Session encountered an error
                IF session.error.code equals NewgroundsIO.Errors.EXPIRED_SESSION THEN
                    COMMENT: The server rejected this session id. Report EXPIRED rather
                    COMMENT: than a generic ERROR, so callers can tell "start over" apart
                    COMMENT: from "something broke", and clear the session-scoped data
                    COMMENT: that is no longer valid.
                    CALL onSessionCleared()
                    SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.EXPIRED
                ELSE IF session.error.code equals NewgroundsIO.Errors.CANCELLED_SESSION THEN
                    COMMENT: User specifically cancelled the session
                    CALL onSessionCleared()
                    SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.LOGIN_CANCELLED
                ELSE
                    COMMENT: Some other error occurred
                    SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.ERROR
                    SET sessionStatus.error TO session.error
                END IF
                RETURN sessionStatus
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: === Check if user is logged in ===
            IF session.user is not null THEN
                COMMENT: User is authenticated - they've logged in
                SET sessionStatus.user TO session.user
                SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.LOGGED_IN
                RETURN sessionStatus
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: === Check if session is pre-authenticated ===
            IF session.isPreauthenticated() THEN
                COMMENT: Session ID was provided but user not verified yet
                SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.SESSION_ID_PROVIDED
                RETURN sessionStatus
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: === Check if we've verified this session ===
            IF session.passport_url is empty THEN
                COMMENT: We haven't contacted server about this session yet
                SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.UNVERIFIED
                RETURN sessionStatus
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: === Check if user is in the middle of logging in ===
            IF passportIsOpen is true THEN
                COMMENT: Passport login window is open - user is probably entering credentials
                SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.WAITING_FOR_PASSPORT
                RETURN sessionStatus
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: === Default: session exists but no user ===
            SET sessionStatus.status TO NewgroundsIO.SessionStatus.NOT_LOGGED_IN
            RETURN sessionStatus
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION isStaleSessionResult(resultObject: NewgroundsIO.BaseResult, sentSessionId: string|null) RETURNS boolean

        PURPOSE: Tells the response import whether a result arrived for a session the app no
        longer holds.
        EXPLANATION: A request sent just before the player signs out can come back after the
        sign-out, and even after a fresh session has started. A session result still carries
        the OLD session, and writing it in through setValueFromResult() would put the old
        session back, replacing the new one. A medal or save slot result describes the OLD
        player, and writing it in would show their unlocks and saves to whoever is playing now.
        The response import calls this for every result and skips setValueFromResult() when it
        returns true. The result itself still reaches the caller.

        PARAMETERS:
            resultObject: A result model that extends BaseResult.
            sentSessionId: The session id the request carried, or null if it carried none.

        RETURNS: true if the result must not be cached, false otherwise.

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Treat an empty id the same as no id, on both sides
            SET currentId TO session.id, or null if it is empty
            SET sentId TO sentSessionId, or null if it is empty

            COMMENT: Compare against the id the request went OUT with, not an id in the
            COMMENT: result. That way the check never depends on what the server echoes back.

            IF resultObject.objectName is "App.checkSession" OR "App.startSession" THEN
                COMMENT: A start is sent with no id, so it is current only while there is still
                COMMENT: no session; a second start's answer is stale once the first has landed.
                RETURN currentId is not equal to sentId
            END IF

            IF resultObject.objectName is one of "Medal.getList", "Medal.getMedalScore",
               "Medal.unlock", "CloudSave.loadSlots", "CloudSave.loadSlot", "CloudSave.setData",
               "CloudSave.clearSlot" THEN
                COMMENT: These describe the signed-in player. One sent with NO session describes
                COMMENT: nobody (a medal list loaded before any session existed, say), so a
                COMMENT: session starting while it was in flight doesn't make it wrong.
                RETURN sentId is not null AND currentId is not equal to sentId
            END IF

            COMMENT: Everything else describes the app, not a player, and is cached as usual.
            RETURN false
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION setValueFromResult(resultObject: NewgroundsIO.BaseResult)
        
        PURPOSE: Updates app state properties from server result values
        EXPLANATION: Called when a result object is parsed from server.
        Uses observer pattern to update existing objects instead of replacing them.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            COMMENT: This value may need additional type casting to access child properties
            resultObject: A result model that extends BaseResult.
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Get the type name of this result. For results, objectName is the
            COMMENT: COMPONENT path that produced it - "Medal.unlock", not
            COMMENT: "Medal.unlockResult". Every branch below dispatches on that string,
            COMMENT: so the naming rule in BaseResult.pseudo is what makes this work.
            CREATE objectName AS resultObject.objectName
            
            COMMENT: === Reject data that belongs to a DIFFERENT app ===
            COMMENT: Four components accept an app_id parameter, letting an approved app
            COMMENT: read another app's data: Medal.getList, ScoreBoard.getScores,
            COMMENT: CloudSave.loadSlot and CloudSave.loadSlots. Their results echo that
            COMMENT: id back, and leave it empty for ordinary local calls - so the server
            COMMENT: tells us directly and no request-to-response correlation is needed.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: This object models ONE app: the one the client is running as. Merging
            COMMENT: a foreign medal list here would replace the local list wholesale and
            COMMENT: mark it loaded, so getMedals() would hand the game somebody else's
            COMMENT: medals as though they were its own. The same applies to save slots.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: The caller still receives the foreign result normally - it is only
            COMMENT: barred from the caches.
            IF isForeignAppResult(resultObject) is false THEN
                COMMENT: === Gateway.getVersion results ===
                IF objectName equals "Gateway.getVersion" THEN
                    SET this.gatewayVersion TO resultObject.version
                    CALL markLoaded('gatewayVersion')
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: === App.checkSession and App.startSession results ===
                IF objectName equals "App.checkSession" OR objectName equals "App.startSession" THEN
                    COMMENT: Create session for first time OR update existing session
                    IF this.session is null THEN
                        SET this.session TO resultObject.session
                    ELSE
                        COMMENT: Update existing session object with new data (observer pattern)
                        CALL this.session.importFromObject(resultObject.session)
                    END IF
                
                    COMMENT: if we got any errors, copy them to the session for handling
                    SET this.session.error TO resultObject.error
                
                    COMMENT: Mark session as verified if it's valid (not expired, no error)
                    IF this.session.expired is false AND this.session.error is null THEN
                        SET this.session.verified TO true
                    END IF
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: === App.getCurrentVersion results ===
                IF objectName equals "App.getCurrentVersion" THEN
                    SET this.currentVersion TO resultObject.current_version
                    SET this.clientDeprecated TO resultObject.client_deprecated
                    CALL markLoaded('currentVersion')
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: === App.getHostLicense results ===
                IF objectName equals "App.getHostLicense" THEN
                    SET this.hostApproved TO resultObject.host_approved
                    CALL markLoaded('hostApproved')
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: A component that FAILED still reaches this function - it produces
                COMMENT: a result model carrying an error and no payload. Every branch below
                COMMENT: therefore checks its payload before caching or merging it. Skipping
                COMMENT: that check is not a style matter: a rejected Medal.unlock has no
                COMMENT: medal, so reading resultObject.medal.id throws, and if that
                COMMENT: exception escapes this function nothing after it runs - the session
                COMMENT: bookkeeping at the end, and in a batched request every remaining
                COMMENT: result.

                COMMENT: THE THREE LIST RESULTS - CloudSave.loadSlots, Medal.getList and
                COMMENT: ScoreBoard.getBoards - are COMPLETE SNAPSHOTS. Each returns the
                COMMENT: app's entire set of that thing on every call: the same ids, the
                COMMENT: same count. An empty save slot is still in the list (a SaveSlot
                COMMENT: with url null), not an omission. So on a refresh (the ELSE branch
                COMMENT: in each) every incoming entry matches a cached one by id and the
                COMMENT: merge loop covers the whole list - there is nothing unmatched to
                COMMENT: handle. importFromObject() OVERWRITES every field, so a slot
                COMMENT: filled or cleared elsewhere, a newly unlocked medal, changed
                COMMENT: board metadata all land, and no stale value survives. Update in
                COMMENT: place - do NOT replace the array - or references the game holds
                COMMENT: (getSaveSlot(2), a medal bound to a HUD) go dead. An id on one
                COMMENT: side but not the other is out of scope here; it means the set
                COMMENT: itself changed mid-session, which warrants a re-init.

                COMMENT: === CloudSave.loadSlots results ===
                IF objectName equals "CloudSave.loadSlots" THEN
                    COMMENT: Counted, so loadData() can tell a slot list came back. A missing
                    COMMENT: payload means the gateway refused the call, which is the offline or
                    COMMENT: signed-out case the local fallback exists for, so it is merged like
                    COMMENT: any other rather than dropped. See SAVE SLOT LOCAL FALLBACK at the
                    COMMENT: end of this file.
                    SET this.slotListsMerged TO this.slotListsMerged + 1
                    CALL this.applySlotList(resultObject.slots)
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: === CloudSave.loadSlot / setData / clearSlot results ===
                IF objectName equals "CloudSave.loadSlot" OR
                   objectName equals "CloudSave.setData" OR
                   objectName equals "CloudSave.clearSlot" THEN
                    COMMENT: Only update if saveSlots have been loaded
                    IF this.saveSlots is not null AND resultObject.slot is not null THEN
                        FOR EACH saveSlot IN this.saveSlots
                            COMMENT: Find matching slot by ID and update it
                            IF saveSlot.id equals resultObject.slot.id THEN
                                CALL saveSlot.importFromObject(resultObject.slot)
                            END IF
                        END FOR
                    END IF
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: === Medal.getList results ===
                IF objectName equals "Medal.getList" THEN
                    COMMENT: No payload means the call failed - see the note above
                    IF resultObject.medals is null THEN
                        RETURN
                    END IF

                    IF this.medals is null THEN
                        COMMENT: First time loading medals
                        SET this.medals TO resultObject.medals
                        CALL markLoaded('medals')
                    ELSE
                        COMMENT: Update existing medals with new data
                        FOR EACH newMedal IN resultObject.medals
                            FOR EACH existingMedal IN this.medals
                                COMMENT: Find matching medal by ID and update it
                                IF existingMedal.id equals newMedal.id THEN
                                    CALL existingMedal.importFromObject(newMedal)
                                END IF
                            END FOR
                        END FOR
                    END IF
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: === Medal.getMedalScore results ===
                IF objectName equals "Medal.getMedalScore" THEN
                    SET this.medalScore TO resultObject.medal_score
                    CALL markLoaded('medalScore')
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: === Medal.unlock results ===
                IF objectName equals "Medal.unlock" THEN
                    COMMENT: Only trust this result when the unlock actually succeeded.
                    COMMENT: A rejected unlock (unknown medal id, no session) carries no
                    COMMENT: medal, and reports medal_score as its 0 default - applying that
                    COMMENT: would wipe the cached total. Reading resultObject.medal.id
                    COMMENT: without this guard is the null dereference described above.
                    IF resultObject.medal is not null THEN
                        SET this.medalScore TO resultObject.medal_score
                        CALL markLoaded('medalScore')

                        COMMENT: Update the unlocked medal in our medals list if available
                        IF this.medals is not null THEN
                            FOR EACH medal IN this.medals
                                COMMENT: Find matching medal by ID and update it
                                IF medal.id equals resultObject.medal.id THEN
                                    CALL medal.importFromObject(resultObject.medal)
                                END IF
                            END FOR
                        END IF
                    END IF
                END IF
            
                COMMENT: === ScoreBoard.getBoards results ===
                IF objectName equals "ScoreBoard.getBoards" THEN
                    COMMENT: No payload means the call failed - see the note above
                    IF resultObject.scoreboards is null THEN
                        RETURN
                    END IF

                    IF this.scoreBoards is null THEN
                        COMMENT: First time loading scoreboards
                        SET this.scoreBoards TO resultObject.scoreboards
                        CALL markLoaded('scoreBoards')
                    ELSE
                        COMMENT: Update existing scoreboards with new data
                        FOR EACH newBoard IN resultObject.scoreboards
                            FOR EACH existingBoard IN this.scoreBoards
                                COMMENT: Find matching board by ID and update it
                                IF existingBoard.id equals newBoard.id THEN
                                    CALL existingBoard.importFromObject(newBoard)
                                END IF
                            END FOR
                        END FOR
                    END IF
                END IF
            
            END IF

            COMMENT: === Always check session remember flag and passport status ===
            IF this.session is not null AND this.session.remember is true THEN
                COMMENT: Save session ID for next app start
                CREATE expirationTime AS CURRENT_TIME + 30 DAYS
                CALL SAVE_TO_PERSISTENT_STORAGE(this.sessionStorageKey, this.session.id, expirationTime)
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Check if passport login is still in progress
            IF this.passportIsOpen is true THEN
                COMMENT: Determine if passport is still open based on session state.
                COMMENT: These must be a single chain, not three independent checks: the
                COMMENT: first branch is reached precisely when there is no session to
                COMMENT: interrogate, so falling through to this.session.expired reads a
                COMMENT: property off null. That happens exactly when a login is
                COMMENT: cancelled while Passport is open.
                IF this.session is null OR this.session.id is empty THEN
                    COMMENT: Session was reset/cleared
                    SET this.passportIsOpen TO false
                ELSE IF this.session.expired is true THEN
                    COMMENT: Session expired while waiting
                    SET this.passportIsOpen TO false
                ELSE IF this.session.user is not null THEN
                    COMMENT: User has successfully logged in
                    SET this.passportIsOpen TO false
                END IF
            END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION isForeignAppResult(resultObject: NewgroundsIO.BaseResult): boolean

        PURPOSE: Report whether a result carries data loaded from another app.

        WHY: setValueFromResult() caches results into properties that describe the
        app this client is running as. A cross-app lookup returns somebody else's
        medals or save slots, which must not overwrite them.

        PARAMETERS:
            resultObject: The result model to inspect

        RETURNS: true if the result belongs to a different app

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Only the four cross-app-capable results declare app_id at all
            IF resultObject is null OR resultObject has no app_id property THEN
                RETURN false
            END IF

            CREATE sourceAppId AS resultObject.app_id

            COMMENT: Empty means "this is our own data" - the common case
            IF sourceAppId is null OR sourceAppId is empty THEN
                RETURN false
            END IF

            COMMENT: The gateway only sets this for external lookups, but compare
            COMMENT: against our own id anyway. A server that echoed the local id on
            COMMENT: every call would otherwise make every result look foreign and
            COMMENT: silently switch off all caching.
            IF resultObject.core is not null AND sourceAppId equals resultObject.core.appId THEN
                RETURN false
            END IF

            RETURN true

    END FUNCTION

    
    ====================
    PRIVATE METHODS
    ====================
    
    FUNCTION markLoaded(propertyName: string)
        
        PURPOSE: Records that a property has been loaded from the server
        WHY: Used internally to track which data properties have been loaded
        
        PARAMETERS:
            propertyName: Name of the property that has been loaded
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Validate that this is a valid property name
            IF propertyName NOT in dataProperties THEN
                THROW error "Unknown property name: " + propertyName
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Check if already marked as loaded
            IF propertyName in dataLoaded THEN
                COMMENT: Already marked as loaded, nothing to do
                RETURN
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Mark this property as loaded
            APPEND propertyName TO dataLoaded
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION onSessionCleared()
        
        PURPOSE: Clears session-specific data from all affected objects
        WHY: When a session expires or is cancelled, we need to reset objects to their
        unauthenticated state while preserving the cached data structure
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Clear the session itself
            CALL session.clearSessionData()
            
            COMMENT: If save slots have been loaded, clear session data from each
            IF saveSlots is not null THEN
                FOR EACH saveSlot IN saveSlots
                    CALL saveSlot.clearSessionData()
                END FOR
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: If medals have been loaded, clear session data from each
            IF medals is not null THEN
                FOR EACH medal IN medals
                    CALL medal.clearSessionData()
                END FOR
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Reset medal score and passport flag
            SET medalScore TO 0
            SET passportIsOpen TO false
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION clearSession()
        
        PURPOSE: Completely clear the current session (used when logging out)
        WHY: When user logs out, nothing that described them may survive. The
             next player on the same device would otherwise see their medal
             unlocks, and a sign-out while Passport was open would leave
             passportIsOpen true, so openPassport() refuses to open it again.

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Reset the session object and all session-scoped cached data
            CALL onSessionCleared()

            COMMENT: Drop any error left over from the old session, so a fresh
            COMMENT: session isn't immediately judged by the old one's failure
            SET session.error TO null

            COMMENT: Also remove the saved session from persistent storage
            COMMENT: So next time they open the app, they won't be auto-logged-in
            CALL CLEAR_FROM_PERSISTENT_STORAGE(sessionStorageKey)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION invalidateSession()

        PURPOSE: Discard an invalid or expired session from memory and storage
        WHY: Re-using a dead session id causes repeated EXPIRED_SESSION failures.
             Same reset as clearSession(); kept separate because the reason differs.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CALL clearSession()
    END FUNCTION

    ====================
    SAVE SLOT LOCAL FALLBACK
    ====================

    COMMENT: A save slot is intended to be stored on the cloud, with a local fallback protecting
    COMMENT: it from network loss and server outages. The cloud copy is the primary one, the
    COMMENT: local copy is a safety net, and each slot's `source` property says which of the two
    COMMENT: is currently being described.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: This belongs here rather than in a UI component. AppState is already the save slot
    COMMENT: cache and already merges incoming slots by id, so choosing between two copies is
    COMMENT: that same job with one more source. Build it into a component instead and two
    COMMENT: components each keep their own cache and can disagree, while a game that uses the
    COMMENT: library without those components gets no resilience at all.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: There is NO setting to turn this on or off. Choosing the newer of two copies is safe
    COMMENT: on its own, and a flag would mean most games never get the protection, which is the
    COMMENT: whole point of having it in the library.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: Local copies belong to whoever wrote them: the signed-in user, or a guest when nobody
    COMMENT: is signed in. Every read and write goes through the current owner, so on a shared
    COMMENT: machine one player's local copy never reaches another.

    FUNCTION applySlotList(cloudSlots: Array of SaveSlot)

        PURPOSE: Merges a slot list into the cache, against the local copies

        PARAMETERS:
            cloudSlots: (required) The cloud's slots, or null if there are none to merge

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Reconcile the cloud's list against the local mirror. This produces
            COMMENT: the slot list AND sets each slot's `source`.
            CREATE reconciled AS this.reconcileSaveSlots(cloudSlots)

            COMMENT: Nothing came from either copy. Caching nothing and marking the
            COMMENT: property loaded would make hasLoaded('saveSlots') answer true for
            COMMENT: data that never arrived.
            IF reconciled is empty THEN
                RETURN
            END IF

            IF this.saveSlots is null THEN
                COMMENT: First time loading save slots
                SET this.saveSlots TO reconciled
                CALL markLoaded('saveSlots')
            ELSE
                COMMENT: Update existing save slots with new data
                FOR EACH newSlot IN reconciled
                    FOR EACH existingSlot IN this.saveSlots
                        COMMENT: Find matching slot by ID and update it
                        IF existingSlot.id equals newSlot.id THEN
                            CALL existingSlot.importFromObject(newSlot)

                            COMMENT: `source` is not a schema property, so
                            COMMENT: importFromObject does NOT carry it across. Copy it
                            COMMENT: explicitly, or the cached slot keeps the badge from
                            COMMENT: the previous listing.
                            SET existingSlot.source TO newSlot.source
                        END IF
                    END FOR
                END FOR

                COMMENT: Add any id the cache has never seen, then sort by id. A first
                COMMENT: listing made while offline holds only the ids that exist
                COMMENT: locally, so the cloud's ids arrive later and must not be lost.
                FOR EACH newSlot IN reconciled
                    IF no slot in this.saveSlots has id equal to newSlot.id THEN
                        ADD newSlot TO this.saveSlots
                    END IF
                END FOR
                SORT this.saveSlots BY id
            END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION mergeWithoutCloudList()

        PURPOSE: The merge for a loadData() that got no slot list back from the gateway

        WHY: The cached slots stand in for the cloud's list. They're the last thing known about
        the cloud copies, so an older local copy can't replace a newer cloud one just because the
        network dropped. Merging against NO cloud list would let a local copy win every slot. A
        cached slot describing a local copy says nothing about the cloud, so it's left out. After
        a sign-out every cached slot has been emptied, and the new owner's local copies are listed
        as they are.

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF this.saveSlots is null THEN
                CALL this.applySlotList(null)
            ELSE
                CALL this.applySlotList(every slot in this.saveSlots whose source is not "local")
            END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION getLocalSlotOwner(): Integer
        PURPOSE: Who local slot copies currently belong to
        RETURNS: The signed-in user's id, or null for a guest

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF this.session.user is not null THEN
                RETURN this.session.user.id
            END IF
            RETURN null
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION reconcileSaveSlots(cloudSlots: Array of SaveSlot): Array of SaveSlot

        PURPOSE: Builds the slot list from both copies, newest wins, recording the decision

        PARAMETERS:
            cloudSlots: (required) The slots the gateway returned, or null if the call failed

        RETURNS: The reconciled slot list, ordered by id, each with its `source` set

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE owner AS this.getLocalSlotOwner()
            IF owner is not null AND this.offerGuestSaves is true THEN
                CALL this.adoptGuestSaves(owner)
            END IF
            CREATE registry AS this.localSaveSlots.getRegistry(owner)

            COMMENT: Build across the FULL slot id range - every id the cloud returned plus every
            COMMENT: id present locally. A slot saved while offline exists locally and nowhere
            COMMENT: else, and still belongs in the list.
            CREATE ids AS every id in cloudSlots plus every id in registry, deduplicated and sorted

            CREATE merged AS an empty list
            FOR EACH id IN ids
                CREATE cloud AS the slot in cloudSlots with this id, or null
                CREATE local AS registry[id], or null

                IF local is null THEN
                    IF cloud is not null THEN
                        SET cloud.source TO "cloud"
                        ADD cloud TO merged
                    END IF
                ELSE
                    COMMENT: Compare by ISO 8601 datetime and take the newer copy. The CLOUD
                    COMMENT: wins ties, since a save that round-tripped is the more complete
                    COMMENT: state, and it wins an unparseable local datetime too.
                    CREATE localTime AS PARSE_DATETIME(local.datetime)
                    CREATE cloudTime AS PARSE_DATETIME(cloud.datetime), or negative infinity if cloud is null

                    IF cloud is not null AND localTime is not greater than cloudTime THEN
                        SET cloud.source TO "cloud"
                        ADD cloud TO merged
                    ELSE IF cloud is not null AND cloud.url is not null AND cloud.url is not empty THEN
                        COMMENT: The local copy is newer, but the cloud holds a save too, so
                        COMMENT: either choice loses one of them. Never decide this for the
                        COMMENT: player: mark the conflict and let the game ask. The slot keeps
                        COMMENT: the cloud's fields, and loading it returns the local copy until
                        COMMENT: the game calls keepLocal() or keepCloud().
                        SET cloud.source TO "conflict"
                        ADD cloud TO merged
                    ELSE
                        ADD this.buildLocalSlot(id, local) TO merged
                    END IF
                END IF
            END FOR

            RETURN merged

        NOTE: RECORD THE DECISION AND HAVE LOADING CONSULT IT. `source` is that record, and it is
        the same property a game reads to draw its cloud badge, so there is only one answer and a
        row's badge cannot disagree with the copy a load returns. If loading recomputed freshness
        for itself the two calculations could differ, and a row would show a cloud badge while the
        load quietly read the local copy.

        NOTE: SYNC IS PASSIVE. Never push a fresher local copy to the cloud on its own. It gets
        there on the player's next explicit save, or when the game resolves a conflict with
        SaveSlot.keepLocal(), and nowhere else.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION adoptGuestSaves(owner: Integer)

        PURPOSE: Moves guest copies into the signed-in player's own local copies

        PARAMETERS:
            owner: (required) The signed-in user's id

        WHY: A guest copy goes to whoever signs in next, and ONLY to them. Once it has been
        offered it is removed from the guest copies, so the player after them never gets it too.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE guestRegistry AS this.localSaveSlots.getRegistry(null)
            FOR EACH id, guest IN guestRegistry
                CREATE payload AS this.localSaveSlots.getPayload(id, null)
                IF payload is not null THEN
                    CREATE own AS this.localSaveSlots.getRegistry(owner)[id], or null
                    COMMENT: The guest copy replaces the player's own only if it is newer.
                    COMMENT: Otherwise it is simply dropped below.
                    IF own is null OR PARSE_DATETIME(guest.datetime) is greater than PARSE_DATETIME(own.datetime) THEN
                        IF this.localSaveSlots.writeEntry(id, payload, owner, guest.datetime) is false THEN
                            COMMENT: Keep the guest copy if it can't be moved, rather than
                            COMMENT: losing it.
                            CONTINUE
                        END IF
                    END IF
                END IF
                CALL this.localSaveSlots.deleteEntry(id, null)
            END FOR
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION buildLocalSlot(id: Integer, entry: Object): SaveSlot

        PURPOSE: Builds a SaveSlot describing the local copy

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Built through the object factory, which is why this lives here and not in
            COMMENT: the store: building models needs core, and that is AppState's job.
            CREATE slot AS OBJECT_FACTORY.createObject("SaveSlot", {
                id: id,
                size: entry.size,
                datetime: entry.datetime,
                timestamp: entry.datetime as a unix timestamp, or 0 if it will not parse,
                url: null
            }, this.core)

            SET slot.source TO "local"
            RETURN slot

        NOTE: A local-only slot carries NO url. There is nothing to fetch, and inventing one
        would send loadDataRaw() after a file that does not exist. This is the one place the
        parallel between the local store and the cloud API genuinely breaks down.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION readLocalSlotData(id: Integer): String
        PURPOSE: Reads the current owner's local copy of one slot
        RETURNS: The stored data, or null if this slot has no local copy
        WHY: Called by SaveSlot.loadDataRaw() and SaveSlot.keepLocal()

        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN this.localSaveSlots.getPayload(id, this.getLocalSlotOwner())
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION getLocalSlotEntry(id: Integer): Object
        PURPOSE: Describes the current owner's local copy of one slot
        RETURNS: An object with that copy's size and datetime, or null if there is none
        WHY: Called by SaveSlot.getLocalCopy(), so a game can show the player both copies of a
        slot in conflict

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE entry AS this.localSaveSlots.getRegistry(this.getLocalSlotOwner())[id], or null
            IF entry is null THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF
            RETURN { size: entry.size, datetime: entry.datetime }
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION writeLocalSlotData(id: Integer, data: String, datetime: String): Boolean
        PURPOSE: Mirrors one slot's save data locally, for the current owner
        RETURNS: True if the write landed, false if it did not
        WHY: Called by SaveSlot.saveDataRaw() for the local leg of a dual write, by
        SaveSlot.loadDataRaw() for its write-through cache, and by SaveSlot.onWriteComplete() to
        re-stamp a save the cloud accepted

        PARAMETERS:
            datetime: Optional. Defaults to now. Pass the CLOUD's datetime when caching a cloud
                      load, or the cached copy looks newer than the copy it came from.

        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN this.localSaveSlots.writeEntry(id, data, this.getLocalSlotOwner(), datetime)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION clearLocalSlotData(id: Integer): Boolean
        PURPOSE: Drops the current owner's local copy of one slot
        RETURNS: True if it was dropped, false if the write failed
        WHY: Called by SaveSlot.clearData() and SaveSlot.keepCloud()

        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN this.localSaveSlots.deleteEntry(id, this.getLocalSlotOwner())
    END FUNCTION

END CLASS

COMMENT: ============================================================================
COMMENT: LocalSaveSlotStore is written here, at the end of AppState, because it is
COMMENT: private to AppState and has no public surface of its own. If a separate file
COMMENT: is more idiomatic in your language, split it out - just keep it private.
COMMENT: ============================================================================

CLASS LocalSaveSlotStore
    DESCRIPTION: The local mirror of one app's save slots
    NAMESPACE: NewgroundsIO
    NOTE: Private to AppState, which constructs it and is its only caller

    PURPOSE: Owns the local copy and NOTHING else: keys, App ID and owner scoping, the registry
    and payload split, serialization, corrupt data handling, and datetime stamping. It knows
    nothing about the cloud, about merging, or about which copy is newer. AppState decides all
    of that.

    OWNERS: Every method takes an `owner`: the id of the user the copy belongs to, or null for a
    guest. Each owner gets its own keys, so one player's save never overwrites or shows up as
    another's. Guest keys are the unscoped ones.

    SHAPE: Mirror the cloud API's DATA shape, not its TRANSPORT. Everything here is synchronous,
    and it returns plain slot data rather than model instances, because building models goes
    through the object factory and needs core. Do NOT give it fake response envelopes or
    callbacks to make it look more like a gateway call than it is.

    ====================
    PROPERTIES
    ====================

    PRIVATE appId: String
        PURPOSE: Scopes every storage key
        WHY: Storage keys MUST contain the App ID, exactly as AppState.sessionStorageKey does.
        Apps on the same host share a storage space, so an unqualified key collides across every
        game using this library there.

    ====================
    METHODS
    ====================

    FUNCTION keyPrefix(owner: Integer): String
        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE prefix AS "ngio-local-save-slots-for-" + this.appId
            IF owner is not null THEN
                SET prefix TO prefix + ":user:" + owner
            END IF
            RETURN prefix
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION registryKey(owner: Integer): String
        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN this.keyPrefix(owner) + ":registry"
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION payloadKey(id: Integer, owner: Integer): String
        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN this.keyPrefix(owner) + ":slot:" + id
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION getRegistry(owner: Integer): Map of Integer to Object

        PURPOSE: Every locally mirrored slot's metadata, keyed by slot id

        WHY TWO KEYS: The registry (small, metadata only) and the payloads (the save data,
        potentially large) live under SEPARATE keys, one payload key per slot. This mirrors the
        gateway's own split between CloudSave.loadSlots, which returns metadata for every slot,
        and CloudSave.loadSlot, which returns one slot's data. It means writing one slot's
        payload never rewrites every other slot's metadata.

        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                CREATE raw AS STORAGE_GET(this.registryKey(owner))
                IF raw is null OR raw is empty THEN
                    RETURN an empty map
                END IF
                CREATE parsed AS JSON_DECODE(raw)
                IF parsed is not a map THEN
                    RETURN an empty map
                END IF
                RETURN parsed
            CATCH
                COMMENT: Unparseable stored data is treated as ABSENT, not fatal. A corrupt
                COMMENT: registry reads as an empty one and the app carries on against the cloud.
                RETURN an empty map
            END TRY
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION getPayload(id: Integer, owner: Integer): String
        PURPOSE: The raw save data for one slot, or null if there is no local copy

        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                RETURN STORAGE_GET(this.payloadKey(id, owner))
            CATCH
                RETURN null
            END TRY
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION writeEntry(id: Integer, data: String, owner: Integer, datetime: String): Boolean

        PURPOSE: Mirrors one slot locally, stamped so the merge can compare it against the cloud

        PARAMETERS:
            datetime: Optional, defaults to now. A fresh save wants now; a write-through cache of
                      a cloud load passes the CLOUD's datetime instead, so caching a slot never
                      makes the local copy look newer than the copy it came from.

        RETURNS: True if the write landed, false if it did not

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF datetime is not provided THEN
                SET datetime TO the current time in ISO 8601 format
            END IF

            TRY
                COMMENT: Write the PAYLOAD BEFORE THE REGISTRY. If the payload write fails,
                COMMENT: usually on quota because it is the larger of the two, the registry is not
                COMMENT: left claiming a slot holds data that was never stored.
                CALL STORAGE_SET(this.payloadKey(id, owner), data)

                CREATE registry AS this.getRegistry(owner)
                SET registry[id] TO { size: length of data, datetime: datetime, hasData: true }
                CALL STORAGE_SET(this.registryKey(owner), JSON_ENCODE(registry))
                RETURN true
            CATCH
                COMMENT: Report a failed write, do NOT throw. Quota limits, private browsing, and
                COMMENT: storage disabled by the user are all real, and a failed local write is a
                COMMENT: leg the caller weighs against the cloud leg rather than an error.
                RETURN false
            END TRY
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION deleteEntry(id: Integer, owner: Integer): Boolean
        PURPOSE: Drops one slot's local copy
        RETURNS: True if it was dropped, false if the write failed

        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                CREATE registry AS this.getRegistry(owner)
                REMOVE id FROM registry
                CALL STORAGE_SET(this.registryKey(owner), JSON_ENCODE(registry))
                CALL STORAGE_REMOVE(this.payloadKey(id, owner))
                RETURN true
            CATCH
                RETURN false
            END TRY

        NOTE: Registry first here. The payload is the larger write, and an orphaned payload with
        no registry entry reads as absent anyway.
    END FUNCTION

END CLASS
